caption: Stamping the import time
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes/stamp-import-time
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Imported tiddlers get `created` and `modified` at ''Apply'', set to the
moment of import, unless the profile binds those fields itself — so
they appear under Recent, and a re-import that overwrites keeps the
original `created`.  Nothing to write for the common case.

To turn that off, or to add the rarely wanted `creator` and `modifier`,
use the `stamp` key (or the checkboxes under the editor's records
path):

```
"stamp": []                                   ← nothing stamped
"stamp": ["created", "modified", "creator"]   ← creator too
```

To put the import time in a field of your own, bind the `@now` context
path.  It is already in TiddlyWiki's date format:

```
"custom-fields": {
  "imported-at": "{{@now}}"
}
```

And when the data carries its own dates, bind them — a bound field
always wins over a stamp:

```
"tw-fields": {
  "created":  "{{created_at|iso-to-date}}",
  "modified": "{{updated_at|iso-to-date}}"
}
```
